:PRINT:

:PRINT: Base Config the Topology 

:CMD: config node R0 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R0 router-id 122.1.1.0
:CMD: config node R0 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.0 32
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1000
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R1 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R1 router-id 122.1.1.1
:CMD: config node R1 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.1 32
:CMD: config node R1 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R1 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R1 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1001
:CMD: config node R1 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R2 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R2 router-id 122.1.1.2
:CMD: config node R2 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.2 32
:CMD: config node R2 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R2 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R2 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1002
:CMD: config node R2 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R3 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R3 router-id 122.1.1.3
:CMD: config node R3 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.3 32
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1003
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R4 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R4 router-id 122.1.1.4
:CMD: config node R4 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.4 32
:CMD: config node R4 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R4 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R4 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1004
:CMD: config node R4 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R5 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R5 router-id 122.1.1.5
:CMD: config node R5 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.5 32
:CMD: config node R5 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R5 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R5 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1005
:CMD: config node R5 protocol isis redistribute connected

:PRINT: Base Config done


:PRINT:Configuring EVPN

:CMD: config node R0 no protocol isis interface eth1
:CMD: config node R0 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 192.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node R0 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node R0 distributed-anycast-gateway 00:02:00:02:00:02
:CMD: config node R0 bridge-domain 10
:CMD: config node R0 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node R0 bridge-domain 10 member eth1 encapsulation dot1q 10

:CMD: config node R3 no protocol isis interface eth1
:CMD: config node R3 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 192.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node R3 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node R3 distributed-anycast-gateway 00:02:00:02:00:02
:CMD: config node R3 bridge-domain 10
:CMD: config node R3 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node R3 bridge-domain 10 member eth1 encapsulation dot1q 10

:CMD: config node CE1 interface loopback 0
:CMD: config node CE1 interface loopback 0 up
:CMD: config node CE1 interface loopback 0 ip-address 10.0.0.1 32
:CMD: config node CE1 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node CE1 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node CE1 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node CE1 interface vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE1 interface ethernet eth1 vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE1 no interface ethernet eth0 ip-address 192.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node CE1 no interface ethernet eth0 vrf 0
:CMD: config node CE1 interface ethernet eth0 switchport
:CMD: config node CE1 transport-service-profile tsp10
:CMD: config node CE1 transport-service-profile tsp10 vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE1 interface ethernet eth0 transport-service-profile tsp10

:CMD: config node CE2 interface loopback 0
:CMD: config node CE2 interface loopback 0 up
:CMD: config node CE2 interface loopback 0 ip-address 10.0.0.1 32
:CMD: config node CE2 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node CE2 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node CE2 interface vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth1 vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE2 no interface ethernet eth0 ip-address 192.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node CE2 no interface ethernet eth0 vrf 0
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth0 switchport
:CMD: config node CE2 transport-service-profile tsp10
:CMD: config node CE2 transport-service-profile tsp10 vlan 10
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth0 transport-service-profile tsp10

:CMD: config node CE2 no interface ethernet eth2 vrf 0
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth2 switchport
:CMD: config node CE2 interface ethernet eth2 vlan 10


:CMD: config node H1 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node H1 interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node H1 rtm-route prefix 0.0.0.0/0 0 0 0 2 0 gateway 172.168.0.254 interface eth1

:CMD: config node H2 rtm-route prefix 0.0.0.0/0 0 0 0 2 0 gateway 172.168.0.254 interface eth1

:CMD: config node H3 interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.3 24
:CMD: config node H3 interface ethernet eth1 up
:CMD: config node H3 rtm-route prefix 0.0.0.0/0 0 0 0 2 0 gateway 172.168.0.254 interface eth1

:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.2 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.2 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1
:CMD: config node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 bridge-domain 10

:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.2 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.2 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R3 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1
:CMD: config node R3 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 bridge-domain 10

:CMD: config node R2 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R2 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R2 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R2 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R2 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1
:CMD: config node R2 bridge-domain 10
:CMD: config node R2 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 bridge-domain 10

:PRINT: EVPN Config Done 

:PRINT: Waiting for 50 sec to stablizie the topology
:SLEEP:50

:PRINT: Checking IMET route 122.1.1.0 state on Router R0 at BGP level
:CMD: show node R0 protocol bgp routes l2vpn-evpn imet | include 122.1.1.0
:STEP:1
:PATTERN-MATCH:122.1.1.0        122.1.1.0:10   0.0.0.0:10     122.1.1.0

:PRINT: Checking IMET route 122.1.1.2 state on Router R0 at BGP level
:CMD: show node R0 protocol bgp routes l2vpn-evpn imet | include 122.1.1.2
:STEP:2
:PATTERN-MATCH:122.1.1.2        122.1.1.2:10   0.0.0.0:10     122.1.1.2

:PRINT: Checking IMET route 122.1.1.3 state on Router R0 at BGP level
:CMD: show node R0 protocol bgp routes l2vpn-evpn imet | include 122.1.1.3
:STEP:3
:PATTERN-MATCH:122.1.1.3        122.1.1.3:10   0.0.0.0:10     122.1.1.3

:PRINT: Checking IMET route 122.1.1.0 state on Router R0 at EVPN level
:CMD: show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 imet-routes 
:STEP:4
:PATTERN-MATCH:10    122.1.1.0        L      0.0.0.0        145
:STEP:5
:PATTERN-MATCH:10    122.1.1.3        R      122.1.1.3      145
:STEP:6
:PATTERN-MATCH:10    122.1.1.2        R      122.1.1.2      145

:PRINT:Checking there must be 3 IMET routes in total learned by EVPN
:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 imet-routes | include Total
:STEP:7
:PATTERN-MATCH:Total : 3

:PRINT: Checking 3 IMET routes on Router R0 in BGP global RIBs 
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn
:STEP:8
:PATTERN-MATCH:[3][122.1.1.0:10][10][0][000000000000][32][122.1.1.0]/144
:STEP:9
:PATTERN-MATCH:[3][122.1.1.3:10][10][0][000000000000][32][122.1.1.3]/144
:STEP:10
:PATTERN-MATCH:[3][122.1.1.2:10][10][0][000000000000][32][122.1.1.2]/144

:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | include Total
:STEP:11
:PATTERN-MATCH:Total routes: 3


:PRINT: Extended Communities of IMET Routes are as expected 
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | xinclude -B 3 32\]\[122.1.1.0
:STEP:12
:PATTERN-MATCH:Extended Community: RT:0.0.0.0:10 (type 0x0102 subtype 0x0002)
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | xinclude -B 3 32\]\[122.1.1.3
:STEP:13
:PATTERN-MATCH:Extended Community: RT:0.0.0.0:10 (type 0x0102 subtype 0x0002)
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | xinclude -B 3 32\]\[122.1.1.2
:STEP:14
:PATTERN-MATCH:Extended Community: RT:0.0.0.0:10 (type 0x0102 subtype 0x0002)

:PRINT: Checking IMET Route installation in Data plane 
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include 17002 | count
:STEP:15
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 1
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include 17003 | count
:STEP:16
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 1
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include 17003
:STEP:17
:PATTERN-MATCH:labels=145,17003
:STEP:18
:PATTERN-MATCH:EVPN-CP
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include 17002
:STEP:19
:PATTERN-MATCH:145,17002
:STEP:20
:PATTERN-MATCH:EVPN-CP
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include Total
:STEP:21
:PATTERN-MATCH:Total MAC entries: 1

:TESTCASE-END:1



:TESTCASE-BEGIN:2
:DESC: Test case to test EVPN MAC-IP Routes Installation 

:PRINT: Topology to be loaded cross_link_topology()
:PRINT: Config to be used from previous TC 

:PRINT: Generating MAC-IP routes by starting traffic 
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
:CMD:run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2

:PRINT: Waiting for MAC-IP Routes generation 
:SLEEP:30

:PRINT: Checking MAC-IP routes in BGP Global RIB count, Must be Two 
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | exclude 000000000000 | include 172.168.0 | count
:STEP:1
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 2

:PRINT: Checking MAC-IP routes in BGP Global RIB
:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | include \[2 | include 122.1.1.3:10 | include \[32 | include \[172.168.0.2 | include /280 | count
:STEP:2
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 1

:CMD:show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn | include \[2 | include 122.1.1.0:10 | include \[32 | include \[172.168.0.1 | include /280 | count
:STEP:3
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 1

:PRINT: Checking MAC-IP routes in L2VPN EVPN RIB 
:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 mac-routes
:STEP:4
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.168.0.1     L      0       0.0.0.0        144     0
:STEP:5
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.168.0.2     R      0       122.1.1.3      144     0
:STEP:6
:PATTERN-MATCH:Total : 2

:PRINT: Checking MAC-IP routes in Dataplane ( Bridge-Domain MAC table )
:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include DP | include eth1 | count
:STEP:7
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 1

:CMD:show node R0 data-path bridge-domain 10 mac-address-table | include labels=144,17003 | count
:STEP:8
:PATTERN-MATCH:lines : 2

:PRINT: Checking that the MAC/IP routes are advertised with IP Address also
:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 mac-routes | include 172.168.0.2
:STRING_STORE1:2
:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 arp-suppression-cache | include 172.168.0.2
:STEP:9
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.168.0.2       $STRING_STORE1

:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 mac-routes | include 172.168.0.1
:STRING_STORE1:2
:CMD:show node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 arp-suppression-cache | include 172.168.0.1
:STEP:10
:PATTERN-MATCH:172.168.0.1       $STRING_STORE1

:TESTCASE-END:2

